# AWS S3 Bucket Versioning Configuration via Terraform

This project provisions an Amazon S3 bucket with versioning enabled using Terraform to ensure data protection, recovery against accidental deletion, and data integrity.

## Prerequisites

* Terraform installed locally.
* AWS CLI configured with appropriate credentials.

## Configuration Details

The configuration is defined in `main.tf` within the working directory (`/home/bob/terraform`). It consists of two main resources:

1. **`aws_s3_bucket`**: Manages the S3 bucket named `datacenter-s3-605789677`.
2. **`aws_s3_bucket_versioning`**: Enables bucket versioning to maintain multiple variants of an object in the same bucket.

### `main.tf`

```hcl
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "s3_ran_bucket" {
  bucket = "datacenter-s3-605789677"
  acl    = "private"

  tags = {
    Name        = "datacenter-s3-605789677"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "versioning" {
  bucket = "datacenter-s3-605789677"
  versioning_configuration {
    status = "Enabled"
  }
}
How to Apply
Open your terminal and navigate to the Terraform directory:

Bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
Initialize the working directory to download required providers:

Bash
terraform init
Apply the infrastructure configuration:

Bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Verification
To verify that versioning is successfully enabled on the S3 bucket, run the following AWS CLI command:

Bash
aws s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket datacenter-s3-605789677
Expected output:

JSON
{
    "Status": "Enabled"
}
